---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
---
<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Deload is built by people who've written programs at 11pm and rewritten them by 7am. We're trying to give coaches their time back without taking the craft out of coaching."
>
  <PageHero
    label="About"
    title="We're trying to give coaches their time back without taking the craft out of coaching."
    intro="Deload is one app for the whole coaching job — the programming, the roster, the messages, and the athlete's phone. Built for coaches who care about the work."
    wide
  />

  <section class="wrap pb-24">
    <div class="grid gap-12 border-t border-rule pt-12 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,1.5fr)] lg:gap-16">
      <div>
        <p class="label">Founder</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[1.75rem] font-semibold leading-tight tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink">Derek Miranda</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-muted">Founder, Coach &amp; Athlete</p>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-[42ch] text-muted">
          Two-plus years coaching at Equinox, Precision Nutrition certified, then out on my own with the teams at Sportslab NYC and Fitness360NYC &mdash; programming for everyone from gen-pop and weight-loss clients to marathoners and competitive powerlifters and weightlifters.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="max-w-[62ch] space-y-6 text-[1.1875rem] leading-relaxed text-ink">
        <p class="text-[clamp(1.5rem,1.2rem+1vw,1.875rem)] font-medium leading-snug tracking-[-0.02em]">
          Deload started with my own roster. I was running a stack of tools and leaning on generative AI, and at some point it clicked: AI is genuinely powerful when the person driving it already knows the craft. So I tried to automate my programming &mdash; and it worked.
        </p>
        <p>
          The hard part was everything after the draft. Turning an AI-written program into something deliverable and manageable on the gym floor hadn't really been done &mdash; and honestly still hasn't, whatever the competition advertises. None of them have a true agent. I can see why: it took an enormous amount of work to build.
        </p>
        <p>
          But hyperspecialized AI &mdash; tuned for one niche instead of trying to do everything &mdash; is exactly where I think this technology is heading, and we're still early. My industry needs better tools. Coach burnout is high. If I can build something that takes that weight off while making coaches more efficient and helping their businesses grow, then this felt almost necessary to build.
        </p>
        <p>
          Deload is opinionated on purpose. It's built for coaches who care about the work &mdash; written to program the way I'd program, edit the way I'd edit, and stay out of the way the rest of the time.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
